  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CORE FUNDING TO MISEAN CARA, WHICH PROVIDES GRANTS TO MISSIONARY ORGANISATIONS FOR THEIR DEVELOPMENT WORK IN AFRICA, ASIA AND SOUTH AMERICA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PARTNER: The Redemptorists PROJECT: The main aim of the project is to establish a new Home Based Primary Health Care programme in the three informal communities of Freedom Park, Chaneng and Boitekong. The programme aims to respond primarily to the health needs of marginalised OVC and adults who are seriously affected by HIV and AIDS, and a lack of access to healthcare in general. The programme will also support OVC to attend and stay in school. At health system level, it also aims to improve collaborative health planning at District Level through sharing of health data and lessons learned from the Home Based approach.</narrative>
  </description>
